Phase audit requirements
The cycle for every phase: BUILD, TEST, AUDIT, FIX, RE-TEST, RE-AUDIT, PASS, FOUNDER APPROVAL, NEXT PHASE.
Outcomes
• PASS: every mandatory criterion met, backed by recorded evidence. Founder approval still required.
• FAIL: one or more mandatory criteria not met. Fix, re-test, re-audit.
• BLOCKED: required tools, credentials, terminal, or accounts unavailable. Report the blocker. Never record a PASS.
Evidence required for every audit
• File-by-file review of the code and configuration.
• Requirements traceability to each acceptance criterion.
• Actual test commands and their output, including MT5 Strategy Tester logs where used.
• Build output for MQL5, TypeScript, and Pine Script where applicable.
• Firestore rules emulator results for allowed and denied operations.
• Security findings, defect list with severity, fix evidence, and remaining risks.
• Screenshots of the dashboard at phone and desktop widths, for every state.
Severity
• P0: critical security, capital protection, or data-integrity failure.
• P1: major functional or reliability failure.
• P2: moderate defect.
• P3: minor issue.
No open P0 or P1 may remain at a PASS. P2 and P3 items are documented and reviewed by the Founder.
Rules for the audit itself
• A self-review is labelled as a self-review, never as an independent audit.
• An audit claims a full review only when every relevant file was read.
• No test output is invented. Environments not available are recorded as NOT TESTED or BLOCKED.
