External limitations
These limits come from the market, the broker, or vendors. They shape the design and cannot be removed by code.
• No centralised Gold order book is available through a retail OTC CFD broker. Order-book-style claims are not made.
• Tick volume from the broker is not global institutional volume. It is labelled as tick volume everywhere.
• The system cannot see bank orders, intentions, or private positions. Institutional-behaviour outputs are inferences from observable price.
• TradingView does not provide unrestricted market data access to an external backend. Alert routing and any data reuse must be checked against its terms before design. No scraping or undocumented APIs.
• Economic news sources vary in reliability and licence. Only timestamped, verified sources are used.
• MT5 Strategy Tester results depend on tick data quality and modelling settings, and do not guarantee live execution.
• Demo results do not guarantee live execution quality, fills, or profitability.
• Broker server time and daylight-saving changes can shift session boundaries.
• Firebase and hosting services have their own quotas, limits, and pricing.
• The EA runs only while the terminal and the machine or VPS are running.
